{"name":"Caribbean Pleasure","hex":"#d5dcce","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pleasure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of being pleased or contented; gratification.","A person, thing or action that causes enjoyment."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["pleased to meet you, \"It's my pleasure\""]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pleasure"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caribbean","blocks":[{"text":"The Caribbean is a geo-political region in the middle of the Americas centered around the Caribbean Sea in the North Atlantic Ocean, mostly overlapping with the West Indies. Bordered by North America to the north and also the west through Central America, and South America to the south, it comprises numerous islands, cays, islets, reefs, and banks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png/330px-Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caribbean","wikidata":"Q664609"},{"title":"Pleasure","blocks":[{"text":"Pleasure is an experience that feels good, that involves the enjoyment of something. It contrasts with pain or suffering, which are forms of feeling bad. It is closely related to value, desire and action: humans and other conscious animals find pleasure enjoyable, positive or worthy of seeking. A great variety of activities may be experienced as pleasurable, such as eating, having sex, listening to music or playing games. Pleasure is part of various other mental states such as ecstasy, euphoria and flow. Happiness and well-being are closely related to pleasure but not identical with it. There is no general agreement as to whether pleasure should be understood as a sensation, a quality of experiences, an attitude to experiences or otherwise. Pleasure plays a central role in the family of philosophical theories known as hedonism."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pleasure","wikidata":"Q208195"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/500px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/1280px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/500px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAtlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Languages_of_the_Caribbean.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Languages_of_the_Caribbean.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Pre-Columbian languages of the West Indies. Ciboney Taíno, Classic Taíno, and Iñeri were Arawakan, Karina and Yao were Cariban. Macorix, Ciguayo and Guanahatabey are unclassified.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALanguages_of_the_Caribbean.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg/500px-The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg/1280px-The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb