n islands exist here. On the north, obduction has scraped rocks onto the North American plate (such as in western Cuba). On the east, the Lesser Antilles subduction zone produces volcanism and an island arc. Complex interactions with the South American plate has created islands along the southern boundary. Coral islands are found in insular Colombia near the east coast of Central America.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATectonic_plates_Caribbean.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Johny_Cay.jpg/500px-Johny_Cay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Johny_Cay.jpg/1280px-Johny_Cay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Johny_Cay.jpg/500px-Johny_Cay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tropical monsoon climate in San Andrés island, Caribbean, Colombia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohny_Cay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg/500px-Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg/500px-Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A field in Pinar del Rio planted with Cuban tobacco","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATobacco_field_cuba1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Jayuya.jpg/500px-Jayuya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Jayuya.jpg/1280px-Jayuya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w